---
version: 2.0.1
title: scanning: error, skipped accounts, confirming reset
file: ./test/keyhop_test.gleam
test_name: a_scan_with_an_error_and_skips_renders_test
---
<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4 p-6">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
    Scan your export
  </h1>
  <div class="[&amp;&gt;video]:w-full [&amp;&gt;video]:max-w-[520px] [&amp;&gt;video]:rounded-box [&amp;&gt;video]:bg-black" id="camera-preview"></div>
  <p>
    1 of 3 codes scanned
  </p>
  <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm">
    Discard the codes already scanned?
    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-error">
      Discard
    </button>
    <button class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost">
      Keep scanning
    </button>
  </span>
  <p class="max-w-[52ch] text-sm opacity-60">
    Google Authenticator shows the export on the phone that holds your accounts, so that phone cannot scan its own screen. Use a second device like a laptop with a webcam to scan it.
  </p>
  <div class="alert alert-error" role="alert">
    <span>
      That isn&#39;t a Google Authenticator export.
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="alert alert-warning block">
    <p class="font-medium">
      Skipped accounts:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-inside list-disc text-sm">
      <li>
        GitHub
        <span class="px-1 opacity-40">
          /
        </span>
        alice

        : otpauth doesn&#39;t support this setting
      </li>
      <li>
        bob: no secret
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="max-w-[52ch] text-sm opacity-60">
    keyhop runs entirely in this page and never intentionally writes to storage.
  </p>
</main>
